From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] zaparoo_scanout: accept any 6.18 point release

validate_platform() refuses to load unless utsname()->release equals the
literal "6.18.38-MiSTer", so the module returns -ENODEV on every other
kernel, including the one it was built for. Narrow the check to the 6.18
series instead of dropping it: vermagic already binds the .ko to the
kernel it was compiled against, and a series move (where the mmap
callback's VMA-insertion ordering could change) still fails closed until
the patch is revisited. The machine-compatible and MiSTer_fb device-tree
checks are unchanged.

Upstream: not submitted (upstream qualifies one stock kernel build)
Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c
+++ b/kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c
@@ -69,7 +69,8 @@
 	const __be32 *cells;
 	int len, ret = -ENODEV;
 
-	if (strcmp(utsname()->release, ZAPAROO_SCANOUT_KERNEL_RELEASE) ||
+	/* Any 6.18.y: vermagic pins the build; the series bounds the VMA contract. */
+	if (strncmp(utsname()->release, "6.18.", 5) ||
 	    !of_machine_is_compatible(ZAPAROO_SCANOUT_MACHINE))
 		return -ENODEV;
 	cells = of_get_property(of_root, "#address-cells", &len);
-- 
